pipeline {
    agent any

    parameters {
        string(name: 'CLUSTER_ID', defaultValue: '', description: 'Cluster ID to check')
        string(name: 'TOP_N', defaultValue: '5', description: 'Number of top consumers to report')
    }

    environment {
        PATH = "${env.HOME}/.local/bin/backplane/latest:${env.HOME}/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:${env.PATH}"
    }

    stages {
        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                checkout scm
            }
        }

        stage('Backplane Login') {
            steps {
                script {
                    echo "Setting up Backplane authentication..."
                    if (!params.CLUSTER_ID) {
                        error("CLUSTER_ID parameter is required")
                    }
                    sh """
                        export PATH=\${HOME}/.local/bin/backplane/latest:\${PATH}
                        ocm backplane login ${params.CLUSTER_ID}
                    """
                    echo "✅ Backplane login successful"
                }
            }
        }

        stage('Setup') {
            steps {
                sh 'chmod +x scripts/*.sh utils/*.sh'
            }
        }

        stage('Check Top Resource Consumers') {
            steps {
                script {
                    def results = sh(
                        script: "./scripts/check-resource-consumers.sh ${params.TOP_N}",
                        returnStdout: true
                    ).trim()

                    if (results) {
                        echo "ℹ️  Resource consumption report generated"

                        // Parse results
                        def lines = results.split('\n')
                        def mode = ""
                        def cpuData = []
                        def memData = []

                        lines.each { line ->
                            if (line == 'CPU') {
                                mode = 'CPU'
                            } else if (line == 'MEMORY') {
                                mode = 'MEMORY'
                            } else if (line) {
                                def parts = line.split('\\|')
                                if (mode == 'CPU') {
                                    cpuData << [namespace: parts[0], value: parts[1].toFloat()]
                                } else if (mode == 'MEMORY') {
                                    memData << [namespace: parts[0], value: parts[1].toFloat()]
                                }
                            }
                        }

                        // Build detailed Service Log message
                        def message = """Resource Consumption Report (6-Day Average)

SUMMARY:
Top ${params.TOP_N} resource-consuming namespaces based on 6-day average usage.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
CPU CONSUMPTION (Top ${params.TOP_N}):
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
"""

                        def totalCpu = 0
                        cpuData.eachWithIndex { item, idx ->
                            def cores = item.value.round(3)
                            totalCpu += cores
                            message += """${idx + 1}. ${item.namespace.padRight(40)} ${cores} cores
"""
                        }
                        message += """
Total (Top ${params.TOP_N}): ${totalCpu.round(3)} cores

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
MEMORY CONSUMPTION (Top ${params.TOP_N}):
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
"""

                        def totalMem = 0
                        memData.eachWithIndex { item, idx ->
                            def gib = (item.value / 1024 / 1024 / 1024).round(3)
                            totalMem += gib
                            message += """${idx + 1}. ${item.namespace.padRight(40)} ${gib} GiB
"""
                        }
                        message += """
Total (Top ${params.TOP_N}): ${totalMem.round(3)} GiB
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

ANALYSIS PERIOD:
• Timeframe: Last 6 days (144 hours)
• Metric: Average consumption
• Source: Prometheus metrics

CAPACITY PLANNING INSIGHTS:

CPU Observations:
- Top ${params.TOP_N} namespaces consuming ${totalCpu.round(2)} cores average
- Review if CPU requests match actual usage
- Consider rightsize if usage << requests (over-provisioned)
- Consider scale up if usage near limits (under-provisioned)

Memory Observations:
- Top ${params.TOP_N} namespaces consuming ${totalMem.round(2)} GiB average
- Memory usage trends more stable than CPU
- OOMKilled events indicate insufficient limits
- Unused memory requests waste cluster capacity

OPTIMIZATION OPPORTUNITIES:

1. Right-size resource requests:
   'oc set resources deployment/<name> -n <namespace> \\
     --requests=cpu=<value>,memory=<value> \\
     --limits=cpu=<value>,memory=<value>'

2. Implement Vertical Pod Autoscaler (VPA):
   - Automatically adjusts requests/limits
   - Based on historical usage
   - Reduces over/under provisioning

3. Review Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA):
   - Scale pods based on CPU/memory metrics
   - Optimize replica counts
   - Balance load across pods

4. Identify resource waste:
   'oc adm top pods -n <namespace> --sort-by=cpu'
   'oc adm top pods -n <namespace> --sort-by=memory'

5. Check for idle/zombie resources:
   - Pods with near-zero CPU usage
   - Deployments scaled to 0
   - Unused PVCs

COST IMPLICATIONS:
Resource over-provisioning directly impacts:
- Node count requirements
- Infrastructure costs
- Cluster scaling efficiency
- Scheduling flexibility

RECOMMENDED ACTIONS:
1. Compare actual usage vs requested resources
2. Identify over-provisioned workloads (usage << requests)
3. Identify under-provisioned workloads (usage near limits)
4. Adjust resource requests/limits accordingly
5. Monitor impact of changes over next week

MONITORING QUERIES:
• CPU usage: 'sum(rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total[5m])) by (namespace)'
• Memory usage: 'sum(container_memory_working_set_bytes) by (namespace)'
• Pod count: 'count(kube_pod_info) by (namespace)'

SEVERITY: Info
Regular capacity planning and optimization report.
"""

                        echo message

                        sh """
                            ./utils/send-service-log.sh \\
                                '${params.CLUSTER_ID}' \\
                                'Info' \\
                                'Resource Consumption Report (Top ${params.TOP_N})' \\
                                '${message.replaceAll("'", "'\\''")}'
                        """

                        currentBuild.result = 'SUCCESS'
                    } else {
                        echo "⚠️  No resource consumption data available"

                        // Build Service Log for missing data
                        def message = """Resource Consumption Report - Data Unavailable

SUMMARY:
Unable to retrieve resource consumption metrics at this time. This may be temporary and does not indicate a cluster issue.

STATUS:
⚠️  Prometheus metrics data not available
⚠️  Resource consumption report could not be generated

POSSIBLE CAUSES:
• Prometheus metrics collection delay
• Temporary network connectivity to monitoring stack
• Monitoring stack initialization in progress
• Insufficient metrics history (cluster recently deployed)

IMPACT:
• No immediate impact on cluster operations
• Monitoring and metrics collection continue normally
• Resource usage data will be available in next check

NEXT STEPS:
1. Verify Prometheus pods are running:
   'oc get pods -n openshift-monitoring | grep prometheus'

2. Check Prometheus route accessibility:
   'oc get route prometheus-k8s -n openshift-monitoring'

3. If issue persists beyond next check, investigate monitoring stack health

MONITORING DETAILS:
• Check Type: Automated Resource Consumption Report
• Requested Top Consumers: ${params.TOP_N}
• Check Date: ${new Date().format('yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss')} UTC
• Next Check: Scheduled in 6 days

SEVERITY: Info
This is informational. Metrics data temporarily unavailable.
"""

                        echo message

                        sh """
                            ./utils/send-service-log.sh \\
                                '${params.CLUSTER_ID}' \\
                                'Info' \\
                                'Resource Consumption Report - Data Unavailable' \\
                                '${message.replaceAll("'", "'\\''")}'
                        """

                        currentBuild.result = 'SUCCESS'
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }

    post {
        always {
            script {
                sh '''
                    export PATH=${HOME}/.local/bin/backplane/latest:${PATH}
                    ocm backplane logout || true
                '''
                echo "🔒 Backplane session closed"
            }
        }
        failure {
            echo "❌ Pipeline failed - check Prometheus access"
        }
        success {
            echo "✅ Resource consumption report completed successfully"
        }
    }
}
